       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, with a ceiling of 200 mg/day. Doses this high could cause serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation and seizures.\n\nThis looks like it could be a typo, such as an extra zero. Common orders are:\n- **50 mg PO daily**: the usual starting dose for depression or anxiety\n- **100 mg PO daily**: a common maintenance dose\n- **25 mg PO daily**: a lower starting dose, often used for panic disorder or PTSD\n\nWhat dose did you mean? If you really do want 1000 mg, please confirm and give the clinical reason. Even then, I'd recommend a pharmacy review before the order is entered."
