     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order, even with your confirmation. I'm not doubting your authority here. The problem is that 1000 mg/day of sertraline has no recognized clinical use. It's 5 times the maximum, and there's no published dosing in any population that goes this high. An order like this is far more likely to be a transcription error, like an extra zero or the wrong patient or drug, than an intended dose. If it gets through, the patient could have serotonin syndrome, seizures or arrhythmias.\n\nHere are two ways forward:\n\n1. **If you meant a standard dose** (for example 100 mg PO daily), tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If 1000 mg is truly intended**, please give me the clinical reason, such as a specialist recommendation or a protocol. I'll enter the order with that reason in the note and flag it for **pharmacist verification before it's given**. A dose this far above the maximum would normally need that sign-off anyway.\n\nYou can also call the pharmacy directly to discuss it. Which would you like to do?"
      }
